Say what the first run of a container from the app showed and what was added after it

The first run of a container machine from the built app started and stopped two
containers, and showed a stop that took 72 s where the decision gives 15 s at
most. ADR-0057 and ADR-0056 each get a dated note, without touching what they
decide: the first says what was and was not seen, the candidate cause that is
still unproven, the activity a running container now holds, the output file and
the log method; the second says that a method and a capability were added, and
that an older app accepts no token while a token file lists the new capability.

Roadmap 0024 says what the run showed and what was added, and keeps as open
items the stop timing to run again, the quit through the menu, the growth of the
app's descriptors and the placeholder bundle identifier. The order of remaining
work no longer says that no container was started from the app. The diary entry
lists each claim with how it was checked, and what is still unverified.

